# PART IX — MAKE SURE THE MODEL IS ACTUALLY USED

This requirement is non-negotiable.

Add verifiable instrumentation for the semantic interpretation lifecycle using the project's existing logging or test infrastructure.

It must be possible to determine, without exposing private chain-of-thought, whether:

- The configured interpreter was invoked.
- The interpretation completed successfully or failed.
- A valid intent plan was produced.
- A tool was selected.
- A capability was executed or deliberately not executed.
